It does NOT cover the manifesto text reproduced under data/text/. That text is
third-party content and is addressed separately below.


THIRD-PARTY CONTENT: data/text/
-------------------------------

data/text/ contains text extracted from the official manifestos and programmatic
documents of candidates in the 2022 French presidential election. These works are
protected by copyright, which belongs to their respective authors, parties and
publishers. The Civis project claims no ownership of them and grants no rights over
them.

They are reproduced here for documentary, research and citation purposes: the server
answers questions about political manifestos by quoting them verbatim, and this
requires a faithful, auditable copy of the source text. Three of the 2022 campaign
websites have already gone offline, so this copy also serves as a record of material
no longer served on the live web.

Every document carries, in data/raw/checksums.json and in the corpus metadata:

  - the URL it was retrieved from, and the original URL when that URL is an archive
  - a SHA-256 checksum of the file as downloaded
  - the party and candidate it belongs to

The full list of sources, with titles and provenance notes, is in
ingest/manifest.ts. Running `npm run ingest` reproduces data/text/ from those URLs.

